      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, `bma4_reg_to_odr` will always return a non-reserved value (register value 1..\u003d12), guaranteed by how it clamps its parameter to the valid range initially.\nTaking the result and adding 1 below might yield a reserved value, which is why this branch additionally clamps to `OUTPUT_DATA_RATE_1600HZ`.\n\nI\u0027ve added some doc comments to the reg_to_odr and odr_to_reg functions to capture what the input and output ranges are.",
